      content:
          '**Shoe Lift Prescription (Immediate Conservative Management):**\n- **Amount:** Full 3 cm correction — for discrepancies >2 cm in the setting of scoliosis, full correction is recommended rather than partial\n- **Design:** Combination internal heel lift (1-1.5 cm maximum inside shoe) + external sole build-up (1.5-2 cm) on left shoe. Full-length lift preferred over heel-only lift to maintain forefoot biomechanics.\n- **Footwear:** Athletic shoe with removable insole works best. Custom modification by certified pedorthist.\n- **Gradual accommodation:** Although full correction is the goal, start with 2 cm and increase to 3 cm over 2 weeks if the patient reports discomfort with immediate full correction.\n\n**Gait Training:**\n- Once lift is in place, retrain gait to eliminate compensatory patterns (hip hiking, vaulting, circumduction)\n- Treadmill gait training with mirror feedback\n- Cadence training with metronome\n- Progress from walking to jogging to running as gait normalizes\n\n**Core Stabilization Program:**\n- Address lumbar scoliosis and back pain with Schroth-based physiotherapy\n- Core strengthening: planks, dead bugs, bird dogs — emphasizing symmetric activation\n- Hip abductor strengthening: address left gluteus medius weakness contributing to Trendelenburg gait\n- Flexibility: hip flexor stretching bilateral, hamstring flexibility\n\n**Pain Management:**\n- Hip pain expected to improve significantly with lift correction (eliminates biomechanical overload)\n- Continue ibuprofen PRN short-term\n- If hip pain persists despite lift, MRI to evaluate for labral pathology from chronic compensatory mechanics\n- Back pain: core stabilization program is primary treatment; expect improvement with LLD correction\n\n**Sports Return Progression:**\n- Phase 1 (weeks 1-4): Gait normalization with lift, core strengthening, hip abductor rehab\n- Phase 2 (weeks 4-8): Progressive running program, agility drills\n- Phase 3 (weeks 8-12): Sport-specific basketball drills, cutting, jumping\n- Phase 4 (3+ months): Full return to basketball with lift in athletic shoes',
